This is a relatively routine application of the results from Section \ref{S: pos hom}, most notably Proposition \ref{P: trivial hessian estimate}.  To begin, fix an arbitrary $\delta_{*} \in (0,\delta)$.   

First, note that since $q_{*} \in \partial \varphi^{*}(p) \subseteq \{\varphi \leq 1\}$, the nondegeneracy condition \eqref{E: nondegeneracy} implies that $\|q_{*}\| \leq \delta^{-1}$.  Since $\delta_{*} < \delta$, one can fix an $R > 0$ such that
