	\end{equation*}

Next, note that, at the limit point $q_{*}$, one has that $D\psi_{\nu}(q_{*}) = D\varphi(q_{*})$ by Proposition \ref{P: touching above test function part} and, thus, by the nondegeneracy assumption \eqref{E: nondegeneracy} and Proposition \ref{P: very easy gradient bound}, 
